spec: BACKLOG "Flakes observed" — hedge-timer-leak, filed by hedge-timed-flake

why: `Hedge.start` PUBLISHES after it acts. It forks the attempt and
  only then adds the fiber to the list settle cancels, and it arms the
  timer only after that. A settle in either window leaves something
  behind: an attempt nobody cancels (a duplicate request that outlives
  the answer — the serious one) or a timer nobody disarms.

what: re-check `done` after each publication and undo — cancel the
  fiber, cancel the timer. A deterministic test drives the window with
  a Scheduler wrapper whose fork lets the first attempt settle before
  the second is registered, and asserts the second fiber was cancelled.

next: write the failing test first, then the fix
